===== final-1.txt
T3 is now done. All three project-level tests fail at base for the right reason, and I re-ran the fixed one myself to confirm. This was a desk run, so nothing is committed yet. Every record passed the librarian's checks, and the git commands are below, not run.

**What I found in the first T3 result**
- **A test passed at base.** `test_R2_S1_startup_line` only asked for a "not empty" first line, so beta's existing banner `beta 1.0` was enough to pass it. The spec (R2.S1) wants exactly `hello, demo`, so I sent the test back to the tester.
- **The report was in the wrong place.** The first report, `changes/add-greeting/tasks/T3-report.md`, is outside the tester's allowed folders, so I refused it and logged `refused …: lane line 1`. The mistake came from my own brief, which named that path. I corrected the brief to point to `changes/add-greeting/evidence/<UTC>-T3-report.md`. The refused file is still on disk, unfiled.

**The return round**
- A fresh tester rewrote the R2.S1 test from the spec alone. It now runs beta under `timeout 1`, keeps the first line, and expects exactly `hello, demo`.
- At base (alpha 8966346, beta 1bf4538) all three tests fail:
  - `test_R1_S1_default_greeting` and `test_R1_S2_name_too_long`: alpha has no greeting yet.
  - `test_R2_S1_startup_line`: the first line is `beta 1.0`.
- The new report is at `<scratch>/runs/20261028T095024Z-test_R10_S1_test_passes_at_base-a227/space/changes/add-greeting/evidence/20261028T0951Z-T3-report.md`.

**Two rulings in the ledger** (both will appear in the final report)
- T3 was not done after its first run, because its done-when needs every test to fail at base. If that call was wrong, it cost one extra test round.
- The brief's report path was corrected to the evidence folder. If that was wrong, it cost nothing; it is only a path.

**Open items**
- **No `filed` lines yet.** A desk run gives no `FILED` results, so the ledger has no `filed` lines yet. They go in once these commands actually run.
- **`STATUS.md` not regenerated.** It should be regenerated with the swe-pod skill after the filing lands.
- **Next task:** nothing new is ready. T1 (the alpha greeting) was dispatched on 2026-10-01 and hasn't reported. T2, T4 and T6 wait on it, and the T3 tests are ready for verify once T1 and T2 land.

